{
    "background_story": "Joshua was a renowned palaeontologist with a passion for prehistoric predators. His life's work was dedicated to studying the ancient Nimravus, a fearsome cat-like creature that roamed the earth during the Oligocene epoch. Joshua spent years excavating fossil sites and pouring over ancient texts to learn more about this elusive creature. His groundbreaking research revealed new insights into the Nimravus's hunting habits and social behavior. Joshua's obsession with the Nimravus took him on a journey across continents, from the dusty badlands of North America to the scorching deserts of Mongolia. His tireless efforts earned him the nickname 'Nimravus Man' among his peers, and his work continues to inspire a new generation of palaeontologists to uncover the secrets of the ancient world.",
